.TH "CSSNUMERICVALUE.PARSE_STATIC" "3JS" "August 4, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSNumericValue.parse_static \- CSSNumericValue: parse() static method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]parse()\f[B]\f[R] static method of the
\f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] interface converts a value string into an
object whose members are value and the units.
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This method cannot be called in \f[CR]Worker\f[R] or
\f[CR]Worklet\f[R] contexts \(em parsing CSS text is restricted to the
main thread.
All other methods in the \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] interface are
available in workers and worklets.
.RE
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
CSSNumericValue.parse(cssText)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]cssText\f[R]
a string containing numeric and unit parts.
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R].
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]SyntaxError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
TBD
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
The following code returns a \f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] object with a
\f[CR]unit\f[R] property equal to \f[CR]\(dqpx\(dq\f[R] and a
\f[CR]value\f[R] property equal to \f[CR]42\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B]let\f[R] numValue = CSSNumericValue.parse(\(dq42.0px\(dq);
.EE
